893079b824b106"}], "turbo": {"file": "minimax/music3/minimax_music3_turbo_lora_8step.safetensors", "bytes": 188810064, "sha256": "9722bb8da08da3912a2b6b8fdb173b9d7d4ce01a68818114a8218cfe25d8545a", "steps": 8, "te_cfg": 1.5, "full_steps": 30, "full_te_cfg": 1.7}, "sources": {"sliders": {"by": "ntc-ai", "url": "https://huggingface.co/ntc-ai/minimax-music3-particle-sliders", "licence": "MIT", "checked": "2026-11-02", "card_says": "Text-encoder LoRAs for MiniMax Music 3, 16 sliders. Start at strength 1 and compare with 0 on the same caption, lyrics and seed. Negative strength is not a trained opposite. Selection used four short clips per checkpoint."}, "turbo": {"by": "guillaume127", "url": "https://huggingface.co/guillaume127/MiniMax-Music-3-Turbo-FP8", "licence": "Apache-2.0", "checked": "2026-11-02", "card_says": "LoraLoaderModelOnly 1.0, KSampler 8 steps euler/simple, CFG 1.5-1.7, text encoder cfg_scale 1.5."}, "base": "MiniMax-Music3 Community License still applies to everything Music 3 makes: commercial use shows the name MiniMax-Music3."}, "left_out": [{"file": "minimax/music3/fiona-crapple_ck250_fused.safetensors", "why": "named after a real singer and made to imitate her; the studio makes no real singers' voices"}, {"file": "minimax/music3/fiona-crapple_reg_ck750_fused.safetensors", "why": "the same LoRA, another checkpoint"}], "honest": ["A slider nudges the song toward its name; it does not switch genre or voice on its own. Write the style in the caption as well.", "Strength runs from 0 (off) to 1.5. The author's advice is to start at 1 and compare with 0 using the same caption, lyrics and seed. Negative strength is not a trained opposite, so the studio doesn't offer it.", "One slider at a time: the author did not test stacking them.", "The sliders were converted on this box to the fused q/k/v layout of the text encoder the studio uses; the conversion binds every key (checked on the CPU, 2026-10-10).", "Turbo speeds up only the DiT's sampling (8 steps instead of 30). The text encoder's planning and the audio decode take as long as before, so a whole song is faster, not 4x faster.", "Nobody has listened to any render made with the kit. Proof below is measured by programs only."], "proof": {"note": "One render per group on the same caption, lyrics (studio-written) and seed, measured by programs. Nobody has listened. Wall times are not given: these ran on a lane shared with H3 renders and waited in its queue, so they say nothing about speed.", "measured_with": "ebur128 loudness, librosa spectral centroid and pYIN pitch of the Kim_Vocal_2 vocal stem, log-mel correlation with the baseline render", "baseline": {"status": "success", "what": "the kit graph with no slider and no turbo (the plain Music 3 settings)", "graph": "music_music3_kit_api.json", "seed": 4242, "rendered": "2026-11-02", "seconds": 29.99, "lufs": -14.9, "centroid_hz": 2900, "vocal_f0_median_hz": 293.2, "voiced_frac": 0.848, "sha256_pcm": "b841ccdb61b50c77", "mel_corr_to_baseline": 1.0}, "renders": {"country": {"status": "success", "what": "Country slider at strength 1.0", "graph": "music_music3_kit_api.json", "seed": 4242, "rendered": "2026-11-02", "seconds": 21.04, "lufs": -13.8, "centroid_hz": 2614, "vocal_f0_median_hz": 332.0, "voiced_frac": 0.772, "sha256_pcm": "111222991caab498", "mel_corr_to_baseline": 0.288}, "female": {"status": "success", "what": "Female voice slider at strength 1.0", "graph": "music_music3_kit_api.json", "seed": 4242, "rendered": "2026-11-02", "seconds": 17.72, "lufs": -12.4, "centroid_hz": 2712, "vocal_f0_median_hz": 296.6, "voiced_frac": 0.902, "sha256_pcm": "a6b24ac1fa79e8bb", "mel_corr_to_baseline": 0.305}, "turbo": {"status": "success", "what": "turbo LoRA, 8 steps, text-encoder cfg 1.5", "graph": "music_music3_kit_api.json", "seed": 4242, "rendered": "2026-11-02", "seconds": 16.72, "lufs": -17.4, "centroid_hz": 4225, "vocal_f0_median_hz": 208.0, "voiced_frac": 0.793, "sha256_pcm": "a7b2b2bc93a0ffdd", "mel_corr_to_baseline": 0.348}}, "reading": ["Each slider changed the song: its log-mel correlation with the baseline is about 0.3, where the same settings give 1.0.", "The baseline already sang in a female range (median vocal pitch 293 Hz), so the Female slider barely moved the pitch (297 Hz). This says nothing yet about what it does to a male-sung caption.", "Music 3 decides the length from the lyrics in its planning stage; these takes came out between 17 and 30 s for the same 30 s ceiling."]}}